WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.584 --> 00:00:04.463
♪♪

00:00:05.088 --> 00:00:10.719
I loved that the writers didn’t
back away from showing two women

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:12.221
just not getting along.

00:00:12.221 --> 00:00:13.639
And that’s fine, that’s real.

00:00:14.097 --> 00:00:15.891
Gonna let you guys
get back to it.

00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:18.769
I’m supposed to listen to her?
I have sweaters older than her

00:00:18.769 --> 00:00:20.979
Stella, she’s the new
generation coming up.

00:00:20.979 --> 00:00:23.148
So Alex I think feels Inferior.

00:00:23.148 --> 00:00:25.400
She feels like this
woman wants her out of there.

00:00:25.734 --> 00:00:26.944
But Greta

00:00:26.944 --> 00:00:27.986
(sighs)

00:00:27.986 --> 00:00:29.029
I love her.

00:00:29.238 --> 00:00:31.114
Isn’t it sort of antiquated to
try and nail this

00:00:31.114 --> 00:00:35.535
thing down so firmly?
Isn’t sexually fluid a thing?

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:37.496
Is that what you’re
saying you are?

00:00:37.496 --> 00:00:39.790
I love the scenes between
Bradley and Laura.

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:41.750
Where Laura’s trying
to pressure her to define it.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.628
The feelings emerge and maybe
you don’t know what they are.

00:00:44.628 --> 00:00:46.797
I think that’s so
beautifully written.

00:00:46.797 --> 00:00:49.758
I think what Bradley sees in
Laura is a woman

00:00:49.758 --> 00:00:53.762
who really pushes her to examine
the truth about herself.

00:00:53.804 --> 00:00:54.721
I’m...

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.849
Is Bradley willing to make the
personal compromises

00:00:57.849 --> 00:01:00.602
necessary to really be a
star in this space?

00:01:00.602 --> 00:01:03.230
And give up some of
her sense of self.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:04.940
Or is she gonna go her own way?

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:06.149
Even if that blows up the show.

00:01:07.276 --> 00:01:09.653
I still don’t, I don’t
understand why it’s a bad thing

00:01:09.653 --> 00:01:11.697
for me to call something my
spirit animal.

00:01:11.697 --> 00:01:14.449
Okay, and by the way, a whole
week went by and nobody cared.

00:01:14.449 --> 00:01:15.867
Well, they care now.

00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:17.619
We’re all from different
backgrounds, different,

00:01:17.619 --> 00:01:19.413
you know, ethnicities, races

00:01:19.413 --> 00:01:21.957
and having to deal with an issue
of cultural appropriation

00:01:21.957 --> 00:01:24.918
and the prejudices that they
each have towards each other.

00:01:24.918 --> 00:01:27.170
I thought that was
was fascinating.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:30.924
There are strong
perspectives that differ on

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:34.261
how race is handled, how social
justice should be handled.

00:01:34.261 --> 00:01:38.515
I’m so genuinely grateful that
we can show all the complexities

00:01:38.724 --> 00:01:41.685
I think that Stella would prefer
you think that she’s blind to

00:01:41.685 --> 00:01:44.187
your charms than she’s a bigot.

00:01:44.187 --> 00:01:46.523
The beauty of the writing,
if you can watch an episode

00:01:46.523 --> 00:01:50.027
and you can have five different
opinions about translating

00:01:50.027 --> 00:01:53.030
the intention of these
characters,

00:01:51.445 --> 00:01:52.946
or what is this really about?

00:01:53.322 --> 00:01:56.241
We ask the audience if you see
yourself in that,

00:01:56.241 --> 00:01:59.411
are you cheering along side
Daniel singing that song?

00:01:59.411 --> 00:02:04.166
And then you realize, oh shoot
was that minstrelsy?

00:02:04.166 --> 00:02:07.669
It’s a beautiful way of
asking our audience

00:02:07.669 --> 00:02:09.463
to start having conversations.

00:02:09.463 --> 00:02:12.215
When push comes to shove
and we get to this

00:02:12.215 --> 00:02:13.550
sort of climactic place,

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:15.469
that’s when we really see who
you are and that you have to

00:02:15.469 --> 00:02:16.887
reevaluate everything.

00:02:17.095 --> 00:02:19.139
It’s an honor to play a
character who’s discovering

00:02:19.139 --> 00:02:21.516
things about America
and the world.

00:02:22.059 --> 00:02:25.062
As you, yourself, are having
that conversation.

